color-theme: genetics

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Insertional and reciprocal chromosome transfers](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c01.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C01 | Chromosome Transfer*

LECT01B, source slide 8 | Insertional transfer moves a segment one way. Reciprocal transfer swaps segments.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Bread wheat chromosomes grouped by number and ancestral genome](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c16.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C16 | Three Ancestral Genomes*

LECT06C, source slide 37 | Each of bread wheat's seven groups has two chromosomes from each genome (A, B, and D).

=== layout: big-image

@image

![One nonsister crossover and its four products](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c22.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C22 | A Single Crossover*

LECT08B, source slide 36 | One exchange between the two genes gives two parental and two recombinant chromatids.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Two exchanges between the same nonsister chromatids](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c23.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C23 | Double-Crossover Meiosis*

LECT08B, source slide 40 | The same two nonsister chromatids exchange segments on both sides of the centromere.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Two ways to separate chromatids after a mitotic crossover](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c25.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C25 | Mitotic Recombination*

LECT09C, source slide 6 | Twin spots can form when the daughters become homozygous for different recessive alleles.

@speaker-notes

Follow the exchange between the centromere and both genes. In one daughter pair,
both cells stay heterozygous. In the other pair, one daughter has two _a_ alleles
and the other has two _b_ alleles. These cells can grow into neighboring twin spots.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Four participating chromatids produce a nonparental ditype](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c28.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C28 | Four-Strand Double Crossover*

LECT09E, source slide 16 | Both exchanges occur between the two scored loci.
All four chromatids recombine, giving a nonparental ditype (NPD).

@speaker-notes

Trace both exchanges. The four products contain only the two nonparental allele combinations.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![All chromosome regions compared with separate G-, R-, and C-banding views](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c31.svg)

@caption

*C31 | Chromosome Staining*

LECT10B, source slide 14 | The reference overlays three separate staining patterns. Colors and widths are schematic.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Homologous chromosomes pair at matching loci across an inversion loop](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c55.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C55 | Inversion Synapsis*

LECT13B, source slide 8 | A loop lets matching loci pair when one chromosome has an inversion.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Chromosomes 9 and 22 before and after reciprocal translocation](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c61.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C61 | Philadelphia Chromosome*

LECT13C, source slide 10 | Chromosomes 9 and 22 exchange tips. Derivative 22 is the short Philadelphia chromosome.

=== layout: big-image

@image

![Six Drosophila gamete products with centromeres labeled X, Y, or 2](repo:prototype/assets/chromosome_engine_mini2/c63.drawn.svg)

@caption

*C63 | Gamete Product Columns*

LECT13D, source slide 41 | After a _Drosophila_ X-2 translocation, alternate
segregation yields balanced gametes. Both adjacent patterns yield unbalanced gametes.

@speaker-notes

Trace the two chromosomes in each gamete. Alternate segregation gives balanced
products. The adjacent patterns give products with a duplication and a deletion.
